Part of #36692. Please view this PR in context of changes like https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36694.

`CTransaction` gains a constructor that allows direct declarative construction as an alternative to building through `CMutableTransaction`. `CTxIn`'s constructors gain an optional argument to pass the script witness.

It is a conscious decision that `vin/vout` are passed as generic input ranges and that only *their elements* are copied/moved.
Passing the `std::vector` by value and then moving the *container itself* into place would allow the following:

```cpp
std::vector<CTxIn> inputs = ...;
CTxIn& backdoor = inputs.back();

const CTransaction tx{std::move(inputs), ...};

backdoor = ...; // <- modify `tx`, potentially breaking its invariant
```

In `Consensus::CheckTxInputs`, the inputs are invalid if, for every input coin, either `coin.out.nValue` or `nValueIn` is out of range. However, the current `checktxinputs_invalid_transactions_test` only covers cases with one input, so the sum `nValueIn` is always equal to `coin.out.nValue`, leaving the [following mutant](https://mutanthub.space/mutants/275) alive.
```diff
--- a/src/consensus/tx_verify.cpp
+++ b/src/consensus/tx_verify.cpp
@@ -189,7 +189,7 @@ bool Consensus::CheckTxInputs(const CTransaction& tx, TxValidationState& state,
 
         // Check for negative or overflow input values
         nValueIn += coin.out.nValue;
-        if (!MoneyRange(coin.out.nValue) || !MoneyRange(nValueIn)) {
+        if (!MoneyRange(coin.out.nValue) && !MoneyRange(nValueIn)) {
             return state.Invalid(TxValidationResult::TX_CONSENSUS, "bad-txns-inputvalues-outofrange");
         }
     }
```
https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36686/commits/f8c6cd84e08043f206ca338d0ba7e4dc8bef5214 adds support for multiple inputs in the test helper.

https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36686/commits/133714d1695bc40277b213afd252c3e320cac73e adds a test case with multiple valid inputs, whose sum exceed `MAX_MONEY`, while also having `nValueIn` != `coin.out.nValue`, killing the mutant.

This PR adds coverage for the global PSBT version field validation on decode.

`test_psbt_unsupported_version_field` checks that the PSBT has supported version number into the `PSBT_GLOBAL_VERSION` field.
The test can be triggered with this diff:
<details>
<summary>Diff</summary>

```diff
diff --git a/src/psbt.h b/src/psbt.h
index 5eb5e81428..d90528e01d 100644
--- a/src/psbt.h
+++ b/src/psbt.h
@@ -94,7 +94,7 @@ inline constexpr uint8_t PSBT_SEPARATOR = 0x00;
 inline constexpr std::streamsize MAX_FILE_SIZE_PSBT{100'000'000}; // 100 MB

 // PSBT version number
-inline constexpr uint32_t PSBT_HIGHEST_VERSION = 2;
+inline constexpr uint32_t PSBT_HIGHEST_VERSION = 4;

